{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "054B", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{topology-section-constructible}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:746526399a796322bd06a9c8e23a290b26c54c34fa0f289bbbdda55effff9098", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nConstructible and locally constructible sets are introduced in\nTopology, Section <REF_0001>.\nWe may characterize locally constructible subsets of schemes as\nfollows.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bc9d05dd65623c136ceff9511cbf711e3f665b0e054b19186e09e76b158b3a84", "unit_id": "tag:054B:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "054B", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$E$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$E \\cap U$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$U$", "MATH_0008": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-constructible}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7d70830e539e4c0d816d4045b6ad07905acfc3340b109ce3cd7ade2859e90641", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c712912bd5fc95ce4b726b0da3a474343f2910fc2ef69dc34768bf7c2398f8ce", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nA subset <MATH_0002> of <MATH_0003> is locally constructible in <MATH_0004> if and only if\n<MATH_0005> is constructible in <MATH_0006> for every affine open <MATH_0007> of <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f828e175229cde3c69ad3d65cbb317d648a15474763db64068426c92bba02ba0", "unit_id": "tag:054C:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "054B", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$E$", "MATH_0002": "$X = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0003": "$E \\cap U_i$", "MATH_0004": "$U_i$", "MATH_0005": "$i$", "MATH_0006": "$V \\subset X$", "MATH_0007": "$V = V_1 \\cup \\ldots \\cup V_m$", "MATH_0008": "$j$", "MATH_0009": "$V_j \\subset U_i$", "MATH_0010": "$i = i(j)$", "MATH_0011": "$E \\cap V_j$", "MATH_0012": "$V_j$", "MATH_0013": "$V_j \\to V$", "MATH_0014": "$E \\cap V$", "MATH_0015": "$V$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topology-lemma-open-immersion-constructible-inverse-image}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-quasi-compact-affine}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{topology-lemma-collate-constructible}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fff3b683ad2055698c69e6834d48b72eaf57d5f784f7be17dfec7662a8b09864", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7829be0af05fc01baab13ef90180d595232ea0e51c491efc14763fe9573d3c25", "source_text": "Assume <MATH_0001> is locally constructible. Then there exists an open covering\n<MATH_0002> such that <MATH_0003> is constructible in <MATH_0004>\nfor each <MATH_0005>. Let <MATH_0006> be any affine open. We can find a finite\nopen affine covering <MATH_0007> such that for each <MATH_0008>\nwe have <MATH_0009> for some <MATH_0010>. By\nTopology, Lemma <REF_0001>\nwe see that each <MATH_0011> is constructible in <MATH_0012>. Since the inclusions\n<MATH_0013> are quasi-compact (see\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0002>)\nwe conclude that <MATH_0014> is constructible in <MATH_0015> by\nTopology, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nThe converse implication is immediate.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:abad5188cdf1ff9f4bb96f362278c88cd88e55e81ef496006efef130bb8fea35", "unit_id": "tag:054C:proof"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "054B", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$E \\subset X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\xi \\in X$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\xi \\in E$", "MATH_0006": "$\\xi$", "MATH_0007": "$E$", "MATH_0008": "$\\xi \\not \\in E$", "MATH_0009": "$\\xi$", "MATH_0010": "$E$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-generic-point-in-constructible}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6a9db19393875142cbeda3e744becd41b115c14751cd3616af48d4ab536ca714", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6d5249b4f8d14ee9bb551f69d2cab59597f2a19cd3f9ab70dd5c662c7748c6d1", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme and let <MATH_0002> be a locally constructible subset.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a generic point of an irreducible component of <MATH_0004>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0005>, then an open neighbourhood of\n<MATH_0006> is contained in <MATH_0007>.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0008>, then an open neighbourhood\nof <MATH_0009> is disjoint from <MATH_0010>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2ea57c47805344be7a747c5e33c4050aef680a33382f659b6545122e684c3339", "unit_id": "tag:0AAW:statement"}
